## Objective
1. To construct a Binary Search Tree (BST) in C++ by inserting elements.
2. To find the minimum element by traversing the leftmost nodes of the BST.
3. To find the maximum element by traversing the rightmost nodes of the BST.
4. To display the paths followed to reach the minimum and maximum elements.
5. To count the number of comparisons required to find the minimum and maximum elements.
6. To analyze the efficiency of BST traversal operations.
